{
  "about": "Typical minimum connection times (MCT, in minutes) and transfer rules for the Connection Assistant. The figures are rounded, typical values for the 40 busiest airports by passengers, from airline and airport connection guidance; they are planning aids, not an airline's official MCT. mct: dd domestic to domestic, di domestic to international, id international to domestic, ii international to international. A leg is domestic when its other airport is in the same country (or country group) as the connection airport, or when both are in the Schengen area. transfer_screening: always (every connection goes through security again), international (when the arriving leg is international). The app (FlightKit Resources/Reference/connection_rules.json) and push-sender (supabase/functions/_shared/connection_rules.json) read copies of this file; a FlightKit test fails when they differ.",
